# A function runs once somebody has a closure of it, so it finds what the body has stored in front of the first operation that does more with it than make the closure.
# To hand the closure to a block is more: behind the parameter nobody sees which closure it is, so the call there names none. ScanOfBody::handToBlock() notes the use.
